From 7cd96d019cdb8946bb0853167e9b6c31e3937732 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Assistant <assistant@local>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:28:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Repo hygiene: remove superseded old/ folders; restore
 {{DRIVE_ENDPOINT}} placeholder in quiz.js/auth.js templates

- dashboard/old/, tools/quiz-maker-v2/modules/old/, tools/quiz-maker-v2/templates/old/
  were dead weight: nothing in the codebase referenced them (verified by grep
  before removal), and the current dashboard/master.html, dashboard/student.html,
  and live templates/modules fully supersede them.
- quiz.js and auth.js templates had the live production Drive endpoint URL
  hardcoded instead of the {{DRIVE_ENDPOINT}} placeholder that assign.js and
  video.js correctly use. sync_site_assets() only ever substitutes that token,
  so these two files would have silently gone stale on the next real
  deployment-URL change. check_asset_drift.py now reports both files clean of
  this issue (only the endpoint line differs from live, as designed).
- No feature changes. All 8 existing backend test suites still pass unchanged.
